> urbndv8@ucscb.ucsc.edu (Parenthetical) writes:
> 
> I like the idea of a spell having a probability of reducing your INT and/or
> HP, but how about extending it to all the characteristics.  And how about
> instead of when you read a spellbook, the spellbook disappearing, have 
> reading the spellbook cast the spell.  This fixes one other problem in
> that spells are not only like wands, but WEIGHTLESS wands.

Although I agree with spells causing brain damage, etc, and spell points
being more valuable, it doesn't make any sense to make you carry a spell
book.  In fact, then spellbooks become equivalent to wands, but heavier and
a lot more trouble.  This would make me pick a wand over a spellbook anytime.
A Wizard should be able to know spells from memory and not have to search
through a spell book every time he's in trouble.

